  howpublished = {IEEE Trans. Fuzzy Syst.},
  annotation = {中文辅助译名：缺少 TSK 模糊系统和自适应图的多标签学习},
  abstract = {Multilabel learning with missing labels is challenging in real-world applications and has received considerable attention in recent years. Most existing methods employ label correlations to address the problem of missing labels. However, these methods directly learn label correlations from the original missing labels matrix, which increases erroneous information. Although some approaches use data augmentation to improve label recovery, they rarely explore the relationship between recovered labels and the feature space. Takagi–Sugeno–Kang (TSK) fuzzy system has strong nonlinear modeling capabilities and interpretability, making it a promising model for addressing the missing labels problem. Therefore, we present a missing multilabel learning method with TSK fuzzy system and adaptive graph. Specifically, the TSK fuzzy system transforms the original feature space into a fuzzy space and enhances feature representations for instances with missing labels. Subsequently, the adaptive graph is used to obtain the label correlations and then applied to recover missing labels, thereby learning the nonlinear relationship between the recovered labels and the fuzzy representations. Moreover, the label manifold structure is employed to constrain the predicted labels to have the same label correlation as the recovered label matrix, guiding the prediction of unknown instances for generalization improvement. Experimental results demonstrate that our proposed approach outperforms state-of-the-ar},
}

